From version 2.2.55 the Metin2 Playerbots project is shared under the
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International
licence (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0).

  Licence text:     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode.en
  Licence summary:  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/deed.en

In short (the licence text is what binds):
  - you may play, run a server for yourself and your friends, and share the
    official packages unchanged, provided that you credit the author and
    link to the project;
  - you may not distribute modified versions of the project or of any part
    of it: adaptations, separate distributions, your own versions of the
    launcher, the client, the panels or the server;
  - you may not use the project for commercial purposes.

How to credit:
  Metin2 Playerbots - Tieru - https://github.com/TieruYT/metin2-playerbots - CC BY-NC-ND 4.0

Text and data mining: the author reserves, within the meaning of Article
4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 and the provisions implementing it, the
reproduction and use of the project for text and data mining, including the
training of artificial intelligence models.

The licence covers the work of the project's authors: code, scripts, data,
graphics and documentation. It does not cover Metin2 (Ymir Interactive,
Webzen), the server-file packages, third-party libraries or parts that carry a
licence of their own. The project's packages also contain such files (the
Metin2 client and game data, the files of the server-file packages); the
permission to share the packages unchanged does not cover them and gives no
rights to them. Versions up to and including 2.2.16 were released under
the MIT licence (LICENSE-MIT.txt), and versions 2.2.17 to 2.2.54 under CC
BY-NC-SA 4.0, and they stay under them. Details and the author's additional
permissions (add-ons to the project, voluntary donations towards a server,
recording gameplay) are in NOTICE.md.
